;;; A premise `(says (and (paid ?g)))` loads and never matches —
;;; M1f **W83**, register row `W83/pattern-argument-and`, filed by S1f.7.3 (T1f.7.3.2,
;;; 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two guests, of whom Ann has paid, the fact `(says (paid Ann))`, and a rule that
;;; welcomes a guest it is said has paid, its premise written `(says (and (paid
;;; ?g)))`. No candidate.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A pattern's argument is what a value can be, and `and` heads no fact: refused at
;;; load, at the pattern, one line, on every command. With `(says (paid ?g))` the rule
;;; derives `(welcome Ann)`.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ──────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `52e05fc1`, release: the program loads; the compiler lowers `(and (paid ?g))` as a
;;; pattern over a relation `and`, which no fact holds, so the rule never fires and
;;; the goal has no row, exit 0 on every command.
;;; Refused at load since S1f.7.3 (T1f.7.3.3).

(relation paid Guest :why "{?1} has paid")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(relation says Claim :why "it is said that {?1}")
(relation welcome Guest :why "{?1} is welcome")
(paid Ann)
(says (paid Ann))
(rule greet () :match (and (is-a ?g Guest) (says (and (paid ?g)))) :assert (welcome ?g) :why "{?g} is welcome: it is said they paid")
(solve :hypothesis-relations ())
(query :goal (welcome ?g))
